@startuml poll-follow-up-section
' cumin works - where the "## Follow-up" section of a pull request description ends, for "write the follow-up note".
' Document: poll.md, section on the follow-up note.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:Find the line "## Follow-up";
while (next line?) is (yes)
  if (starts with "# " or "## "?) then (yes)
    :End the section before the line;
    stop
  elseif (only hyphens, three or more,\noutside a code block?) then (yes)
    if (the line before is a paragraph line?) then (yes)
      :Setext heading:
      keep the line in the section;
    else (no)
      :Horizontal rule:
      end the section before the line;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :Keep the line in the section;
  endif
endwhile (no)
:End the section at the end of the description;
stop

note right
  No paragraph line:
  * an empty line, or the line "## Follow-up"
  * a line of a code block
  * a line of an HTML comment
  * a line of a list item or of a block quote
  * a heading, a table row, another rule
end note
@enduml
